Found by karr-pod-writer while documenting Config.pm for #118.

App::karr::Config::status_config has zero callers in lib/ or t/. The lookup it
performs -- find the entry for a status name in _list('statuses') -- is inlined
a second time inside status_requires_claim, which does have callers.

So either status_requires_claim should call status_config and the duplication
goes away, or status_config is dead and should go. The first is the smaller
change and leaves one place where "what does the board say about this status"
is answered; worth checking whether any other method inlines the same walk
before deciding.

It is documented as it stands, so nothing is misleading in the meantime. Filed
because a pod-writer should not silently decide that a public method is dead.
